/artist/19812/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"19812","image":"https://i.discogs.com/Uax0rIyEObKMyBcKDKpvSS4__c5vEL46El6vufYE3Tg/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:455/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE5ODEy/LTE2MzkwMjIyNTgt/OTM1Ny5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/wXzJipGoovTrvUODEqLKskRxGtU71d0AfHVHPPA_qcY/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE5ODEy/LTE2MzkwMjIyNTgt/OTM1Ny5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Born: 15 October 1938, in Abeokuta, Nigeria. \r\nDied: 2 August 1997, of AIDS and heart failure in Lagos, Nigeria. \r\n\r\nHe formed his first group Koola Lobitos in 1963. The large jazz, funk, and afrobeat collective underwent many changes in the following decades but the style remained the same thanks to Fela's vision and other key members such as drummer Tony Allen. \r\n\r\nIn 1969 after visiting America, Fela returned to Nigeria and opened club Afro Spot in Lagos also changing the group's name to Afrika 70. He played with Ginger Baker on the album Ginger Baker Live with Afrika 70 and Fela Kuti, released in 1971 and along side Bobby Gass, better known as Bobby Tench from The Jeff Beck Group, on Stratavarious which was released the next year. In 1981 Fela changed the group's name for the last time to Egypt 80. \r\n\r\nHe was known as Fela Ransome-Kuti until about 1978, when he renamed himself Fela Anikulapo Kuti, the middle name meaning 'he who carries death in his pouch'. He was a human rights revolutionary who started his own political party, Movement Of The People, to protest the kleptocracy in Nigeria. He had his own compound called the Kalakuta Republic in Lagos, which he declared independent from Nigeria, where he and his uncountable number of wives lived and they were constantly terrorized by the government.\r\n\r\nHis influence on funk and African music is unsurpassed and has put his name to many albums, the total number thought to be 77.\r\n\r\nFather of [a3376] and [a727660].","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:19812","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":224273,"name":"Africa 70"},{"active":true,"id":273534,"name":"Egypt 80"},{"active":true,"id":639889,"name":"Nigeria 70"},{"active":true,"id":1453270,"name":"Fela Ransome Kuti & His Koola Lobitos"},{"active":true,"id":1591545,"name":"Fela Ransome-Kuti Quintet"},{"active":true,"id":3012051,"name":"Ginger Baker & African Friends"},{"active":true,"id":4951861,"name":"Fela Ransome-Kuti & The Highlife Rakers"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["A. Kuti","Anikulapo","Anikulapo Kuti","Anikulapo Kuti Olufela Olufemi","F. A. Kuti","F. Anikulapo Kuti","F. Kuti","F. R. Kuti","F. Ransome Kuti","F. Ransome-Kuti","F.A. Kuti","F.R. Kuti","F.R. Kuty","FK","Fela","Fela  Ransome (Anikulapo) Kuti","Fela - Ransome Kuti","Fela A. Kuti","Fela AnIkulapo Kuti","Fela Anakulapo","Fela Anakulapo Kuti","Fela Anikalupo Kuti","Fela Aniklapo-Kuti","Fela Anikolapo Kuti","Fela Aniku 'la' po'Kuto","Fela Anikula-Po Kuti","Fela Anikulapo","Fela Anikulapo - Kuti","Fela Anikulapo K","Fela Anikulapo Kuti","Fela Anikulapo-Kuti","Fela Anikulapu Kuti","Fela Anikulapu-Kuti","Fela Anikupalo Kuti","Fela Anikúlápó Kuti","Fela Anukulapo Kuti","Fela Aníkúlápó Kuti","Fela Aníkúlápó-Kuti","Fela Aníkú˙ápó Kuti","Fela K","Fela Ramsome Kuti","Fela Ramsome-Kuti","Fela Ramsone Kuti","Fela Ransome","Fela Ransome - Kuti","Fela Ransome Kuti","Fela Ransome-Kuti","Fela Ransome—Kuti","Fela Ranson Kuti","Fela Ranzome Kuti","Fela Rasome Kuti","Fela Áníkúlápó Kútì","Fela-Ransome Kuti","Felakutiego","Fella","Fella Cutie","Fella Ransome-Kutti","Felá","Felá Anikulapo Kuti","Felá Anikulapo-Kuti","Felá Anikũlapo Kuti","Felá Anikũlapo-Kuti","Félá Anikulapo Kuti","Fḛlá Anikulapo Kuti","Fḛlá Anikulapo-Kuti","Fẹla","Fẹla Anikulapo Kuti","Fẹla Anikulapo-Kuti","Fẹla Aníkúlápó Kuti","Fẹla Ransome Kuti","Fẹla Ransome-Kuti","Fẹlá","Fẹlá Anikulapo Kuti","Kuti","Kuti Fela Aniklapo","Olufela Olufemi Anikulapo Kuti","Ransom-Kuti","Ransome & Kuti","Ransome - Kuti","Ra